<p>You want to sell. You want to reach new clients.</p>

<p>Whether you are selling a service or a product, you want your online presence to grab a potential client’s attention. Your key market may be in Germany, but you may be seeking to expand into the English-speaking market. Or you may be seeking to attract international clients here in Germany.</p> 

<p>That’s why you want your website to be translated into English. And you want it to read like the original text, not like a translation. </p>

<p>Language Landscapes knows that the translation of your text has a unique purpose – to communicate your line of business to new clients in a way that they can relate to and understand. </p>

<p>Translating your text, however, is only one aspect of what we do. In order to strike the right chord with your target audience, we need to ensure that your brand identity also translates correspondingly. To do this, communicating with you on a regular basis throughout the process is vital. It also means we can develop with you a glossary of company-specific and/or product-specific terminology for consistency.</p>

<p>As part of our quality control process, we check that the translated content fits within your existing site design, returning your website to you in the same format. We also take care to ensure that all links are intact, tags are preserved and keywords optimally localized.</p>

<p>Finally, Language Landscapes can translate Google Ads, Facebook Ads and pay per click advertising campaigns if you send us the advertising text on a spreadsheet.</p>